-- title:
--   w preserves the smooth locus; the model is separated
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $p$ and $M$ with $p$ prime and $M \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a divisibility $p \mid M$. Assume further that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` — the series $q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum` with coefficients pushed into $\mathbb{Q}$, i.e. the $q$-expansion of $j$ — lies in the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the ratios `intFormRatiosC ℚ ⊤` for the full modular group. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, which packages a model of the $\Gamma_H(M)$-curve over the base ring `R p` together with, among other data, the structure morphism `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` — the canonical morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `R p` from the two-chart integral model glued from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebras `chartAlgFin` and `chartAlgInf` of the function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` generated by `jAt` and its inverse — and the fields `w` (a self-isomorphism of the model over the base) and `smoothLocus` (an open subscheme). The conclusion is twofold: the scheme-theoretic preimage of `𝔛.smoothLocus` under the underlying morphism of `𝔛.w` equals `𝔛.smoothLocus`, and `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` is separated.
--
--   The first assertion says that the Atkin–Lehner type automorphism $w$ recorded in a Deligne–Rapoport style model at $p$ permutes the opens that are smooth over the base and therefore fixes the largest such open; the second is the separatedness of the structure morphism of the model. Both are the bundle-specific inputs used by the three lemmas producing two-sided pools of closed primes in the smooth locus (for residue characteristics $2$, $3$ and $\ge 5$).
